ut twelve points Republican. He has raised roughly $1.7 million and holds more than $1 million on hand, while Democrat John Vincent has raised under $300,000. Prediction markets give Fry about a 95% chance of winning.\n\nThe only public poll, conducted in late July by a Democratic-leaning firm, showed Fry ahead by just four points, but its partisan sponsorship and small sample limit its reliability. The overall evidence points to a comfortable but not entirely risk-free Republican win, with the district's lean and Fry's financial edge doing most of the work.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0379, "margin": -13.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0447, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0469, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0326, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0563, "margin": -12.0}]}